& [SchemaGapLedger: P2-S01] is the gap ledger produced by P2-S01
  + [schema_gap] is common envelope must decide whether IR8 manager handoff, human override, refusal, operation dry-run handoff, dependency decision, dispatch deferral, and live-control deferral remain encoded under existing record kinds or require new KernelRecordKind values
  + [schema_gap] is authority vocabulary must reconcile source_only, narrative_projection, accepted_decision, signed_sjs, proof_backed, stale_projection, contradicted, invalidated, and human_override with projection-only, carrier-only, execution-state-only, generated-output-only, dispatch-authority, and live-control-authority distinctions used after IR5 through IR8
  + [schema_gap] is freshness vocabulary must reconcile current/stale/unknown/not_applicable/invalidated with fresh, blocked, faulted, interrupted, pending_review, contested, and dry-run-only projection states used by surfaces, coordination, operations, and manager models
  + [schema_gap] is lineage edge vocabulary must decide whether generated, projected_from, reviewed_by, gates, activates, assigned_to, carrier_of, checkpoint_of, and handoff_to need normalized edge roles before P3 operator contracts consume them
  + [schema_gap] is record-specific payloads must decide how operation_request, dry_run_result, human_approval, resource_safety_review, manager_handoff, human_override, refusal_record, dependency_decision, dispatch_decision, and live_control_deferral records map into existing or new record schemas
  + [schema_gap] is natural-key matrix must decide stable identity rules for manager packet revisions, handoff revisions, override expiration, refusal evidence, generated output proofs, dependency decisions, dispatch decisions, and live-control deferral records
  + [schema_gap] is storage posture remains undecided for truth-bearing kernel records and must not be collapsed into IR2 SQLite projection policy
  + [schema_gap] is fixture oracle must cover valid, stale, blocked, contradicted, invalidated, unresolved-natural-key, hidden-authority, missing-source, broken-lineage, projection-only, and false-ready cases before broad implementation activation

  = must: resolve or explicitly defer these gaps in P2-S02 through P2-S05
  = must: prevent any gap from silently becoming downstream support

& [SupersessionPosture: P2-S01] is the supersession posture for existing schema authority
  + [Kernel_Record_Core.v1.sop] is accepted_boundary_input_not_superseded
  + [Authority_Kernel_Record_Schemas.v1.sop] is accepted_boundary_input_not_superseded
